A checklist would be a good idea.  I should write up a more detailed and up-to-date instruction for Windows users from installing RStan (including R, Rtools, Rcpp).

>
> The RStan instructions say this under the heading
> "R on Windows" in pre-requisites:
>
> "You must override the default install directory to install R in a directory without a space in it"
>
> So I guess there's an alternative to the must here.
> But what I want to do is somehow let people realize
> they missed some of the instructions by presenting it as
> a checklist.
>
> Maybe we could help Rcpp figure out how to work around
> the space issue?  Windows does support paths with spaces,
> so presumably something in Rcpp isn't accessing them
> correctly.

I had asked them to fix it:
http://comments.gmane.org/gmane.comp.lang.r.rcpp/3651

Actually, I did some work in rstan so that it works when rcpp has been installed to a path with space (at least I believe so for rstan 1.0.0).  But I do know in a rare situation it does not work.  So it is tricky to get around the space issue.  I do not mention much that R can be installed in a path with space and so does Rcpp is that I really hope users make sure that Rcpp works before installing rstan.

