A colleague was having a similar problem with a mixture model this week. Can you verify whether there are multiple modes? There are some R functions to facilitate this. If there are multiple modes, the traceplot() function should have as many lines as you have chains that each flatten out but at different places. Also, pairs() of a stanfit-object with optional argument chain_id = c(i,j) will contrast the bivariate kernel densities for the i-th and j-th chains with the lower-diagonal and upper-diagonal of the plot respectively.

Ben

