> I have a question about division operator. In my model, one of the parameters is a K by T non-negative matrix S,
> represented as:
>
> |
> vector<lower=0>[K] S[T];
> |
>
> Each column of S is gamma distributed:
>
> S[t] ~ gamma(alpha, alpha / S[t-1]), where t in 1:T
>
> which is basically time-dependent by setting the expectation as the previous column. Here alpha is of type real<lower=0>
> and is provided. Since S[t] is of type vector,
>
> |
> S[t] ~ gamma(alpha, alpha / S[t-1]);
> or

> S[t]~ gamma(alpha, alpha./ S[t-1]);

> |
>
> is not a valid expression. From the document, it seems that broadcast is supported for "+" and "-" operators. Therefore
> it would be great of "/" is also broadcastable. Now my workaround is to have a transformed parameter alpha_vec:
>
> |
> transformed parameters {
>    vector[K] alpha_vec;
>    for (k in 1:K) {
>      alpha_vec[k] <- alpha;
>    }
> }
> |
>
> which essentially does the broadcast myself by creating a vector with each element as alpha. But as my model is fairly
> complicated, I hope to optimize my code as best as I can (My model is still running, hopefully will be finished by
